{"pageProps":{"fileName":"2026-06-02-location-spot-sydneyoperahouse","title":"Sydney Opera House","cover":"/assets/snippets/location/99fbb935c4595e1c3b494c76a7629add.jpg","tags":["spot"],"date":"2026-06-02","review":"Seeing the Sydney Opera House in person after only ever seeing it in photos was surreal. Our visit happened to coincide with the Vivid Sydney festival, so there was plenty to take in. The night views were stunning, with light installations scattered all around the building.","description":"","series":"location","type":"snippets","postKey":"7957adb446d489f0470f174239f2e61d","content":"\n<center>\n<RestaurantCard\n  cover=\"/assets/snippets/location/99fbb935c4595e1c3b494c76a7629add.jpg\"\n  title=\"Sydney Opera House\"\n  cuisine=\"Spot\"\n  address=\"Bennelong Point, Sydney NSW 2000 Australia\"\n  rating=4\n  tags=\"spot\"\n/>\n</center>\n\n## Review\nSeeing the Sydney Opera House in person after only ever seeing it in photos was surreal.\n\nOur visit happened to coincide with the <mark>Vivid Sydney</mark> festival, so there was plenty to take in.  \nThe night views were stunning, with light installations scattered all around the building.\n```adcard\n```\nOriginally, a show featuring 1,000 drones painting the sky was scheduled,  \nbut an incident occurred a few days earlier where a large number of drones crashed mid-show, and all drone shows were cancelled afterwards.  \nThey were replaced with <mark>fireworks</mark> and a laser show instead.\n\nIt was a bit disappointing, but the fireworks and laser show were decent in their own right.  \nThere was plenty to see and the night views were absolutely beautiful.  \n## Pictures\n<pictures>\n<img src=\"/assets/snippets/location/99fbb935c4595e1c3b494c76a7629add.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\" alt=\"Sydney Opera House\">\n<img src=\"/assets/snippets/location/17baf9d55a63336b28584de461e9b205.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\" alt=\"Sydney Oper